.\" The settings of a self-extracting program (.aqr/sfx/), in mdoc(7). What sfx.toml takes is
.\" crates/aqr-sfx/src/config.rs's `compile`; keep the two together.
.Dd November 27, 2026
.Dt AQRSFX 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm aqrsfx
.Nd settings of a self-extracting program made by aqr
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa .aqr/sfx/sfx.toml
.Pp
.Pa .aqr/sfx/ Ns Ar license.txt , banner.png , icon.ico , manifest.xml ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ql aqr --format sfx
makes a self-extracting program for Windows: run, it writes out the files of the archive it
carries.
Where the root of the input has a directory
.Pa .aqr/sfx/
with a file
.Pa sfx.toml
in it, the program does what the file tells: where the files go, what is asked and told, the
program run once they are written, the shortcuts made, and the icon, version and manifest of
the program itself.
.Pp
The files of
.Pa .aqr/sfx/
are archived as any other, first in the archive (its first segment, which the program reads
before the rest), so that extracting the archive and making the program again from it makes
the same program.
.Nm aqr
reads them back from the archive it made and compiles the settings into the program; the
program never reads
.Pa sfx.toml .
.Pp
.Pa .aqr/sfx/
is taken at the root of an input alone (elsewhere it is data); of several inputs, at most one
may have it at the root of the archive.
Without
.Fl -format Cm sfx
it is archived as files, and told so.
.Pp
A program of no settings writes the files under the working directory (or the directory
given), a file already there failing it.
.Ss Checks
The settings are checked as the program is made, not as it runs: a key not known (a typo), a
value of the wrong type, a file of
.Pa .aqr/sfx/
named and not there, a program to run not in the archive and settings at odds with each
other fail
.Nm aqr .
.Ss Paths
The paths of the archive in the settings
.Pf ( Ic run.program ,
.Ic run.cwd ,
.Ic shortcut.target ,
.Ic shortcut.folder )
are relative to its root, by
.Ql / ,
of names alone (no
.Ql \&. ,
.Ql .. ,
.Ql \e
nor
.Ql \&: ) .
Those of files of the settings
.Pf ( Ic ui.license ,
.Ic ui.banner ,
.Ic pe.icon )
are as such, relative to
.Pa .aqr/sfx/ .
.Pp
A destination
.Pq Ic extract.dest
is one of these places, and a relative path after it:
.Bl -tag -width "{programs}" -offset indent
.It Cm {temp}
a new directory of the system's temporary directory;
.It Cm {here}
the directory of the program;
.It Cm {cwd}
the working directory;
.It Cm {programs}
the directory of programs
.Pq Ev %ProgramFiles% .
.El
.Pp
In the arguments of the program run and of shortcuts, and in the values of
.Ic run.env ,
.Cm {dest}
is where the files went.
.Ss Texts by language
A text
.Pf ( Ic title ,
.Ic ui.prompt ,
.Ic ui.finish ,
.Ic shortcut.name ,
.Ic shortcut.description )
is a string, or a table of them by language tag:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[ui]
prompt = { en = "Install Tool?", ko = "도구를 설치할까요?" }
.Ed
.Pp
The one shown is that of the user's language
.Pq Ql ko-KR ,
else of its first subtag
.Pq Ql ko ,
else of no language (the empty key), else English, else the first.
A file of the settings
.Pf ( Ic ui.license ,
.Ic ui.banner )
is picked so by its name: for
.Pa license.txt ,
.Pa license.ko-KR.txt ,
then
.Pa license.ko.txt ,
then
.Pa license.txt .
.Sh SFX.TOML
A TOML file, of these keys; all may be left out.
.Ss Top level
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic mode No = Qo Cm extract Qc | Qo Cm run Qc
The defaults the other keys change.
.Cm extract
writes the files under
.Cm {cwd} ,
asking before a file there is written over, and ends.
.Cm run
writes them under
.Cm {temp} ,
writing over what is there, runs
.Ic run.program ,
waits for it, removes what was written and ends with its exit code.
By default
.Cm run
where
.Ic run.program
is given, else
.Cm extract .
.It Ic title No = Ar text
The title of the program's windows (its file name by default).
.El
.Ss \&[extract\&]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic dest No = Ar destination
Where the files go
.Pq see Sx Paths ;
.Cm {cwd}
of
.Cm extract ,
.Cm {temp}
of
.Cm run .
A directory given on the command line goes before it.
.It Ic subdir No = Ar bool
The files under a directory of the program's name
.Pf ( Pa setup.exe :
.Pa setup )
there (false).
.It Ic ask No = Ar bool
Ask where the files go, offering
.Ic dest
(false).
.It Ic overwrite No = Qo Cm ask Qc | Qo Cm always Qc | Qo Cm never Qc | Qo Cm newer Qc
What is done where a file is already there: asked (the default of
.Cm extract ;
written over without
.Fl y ) ,
written over (the default of
.Cm run ) ,
left, or written over where the archive's is newer by its modification time.
.El
.Ss \&[run\&]
Only of
.Ic mode No = Qq Cm run .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic program No = [ Ar path , Ar arg ... ]
The program run once the files are written: a path of the archive to a
.Pa .exe
or
.Pa .com
file (not in
.Pa .aqr/ ) ,
then its arguments.
It is run as it is, by no shell:
.Pa .bat ,
.Pa .cmd
and
.Pa .msi
files are not run.
.It Ic cwd No = Ar path
Its working directory, a directory of the archive (by default
.Ql \&. ,
where the files went).
.It Ic window No = Qo Cm normal Qc | Qo Cm hidden Qc | Qo Cm minimized Qc
How its window is shown
.Pq Cm normal .
.It Ic wait No = Ar bool
Wait for it to end (true); else the self-extracting program ends as it starts it.
.It Ic cleanup No = Ar bool
Once it ends, remove the files and directories that were written (as
.Ic wait ;
not with
.Ic wait No = Cm false ) .
.It Ic exit-code No = Ar bool
End with its exit code (as
.Ic wait ;
not with
.Ic wait No = Cm false ) .
.It Ic \&[run.env\&]
Environment variables set for it, each
.Ar name No = Qq Ar value ;
the others are those of the self-extracting program.
.El
.Pp
Of
.Cm run ,
the files of
.Pa .aqr/
are not written out (but with
.Fl -noexec ) .
.Ss \&[ui\&]
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic prompt No = Ar text
Asked (yes or no) before anything is written; no ends the program.
.It Ic license No = Ar file
A license to agree to before anything is written: a UTF-8 text file of
.Pa .aqr/sfx/ ,
by language
.Pq see Sx Texts by language ;
not agreed to ends the program.
.It Ic banner No = Ar file
An image shown above the prompt and the license, in windows (where there is no console): a PNG, BMP,
JPEG or GIF file of
.Pa .aqr/sfx/ ,
by language, at its size at 96 DPI.
Only with
.Ic prompt
or
.Ic license .
.It Ic finish No = Ar text
Told once done.
.It Ic quiet No = Ar bool
Ask and tell nothing, as
.Fl y
(false).
.El
.Ss \&[pe\&]
What is written into the program's own image, which Windows shows before it runs.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic subsystem No = Qo Cm cli Qc | Qo Cm gui Qc
A console program (the default) or one of windows alone.
.It Ic icon No = Ar file
The program's icon, a
.Pa .ico
file of
.Pa .aqr/sfx/ .
.It Ic admin No = Ar bool
Run as an administrator (false): the manifest's
.Ql requestedExecutionLevel .
Not with
.Pa manifest.xml .
.It Ic version No = Qq Ar a Ns Op . Ns Ar b Ns Op . Ns Ar c Ns Op . Ns Ar d
Its file and product version, of numbers 0 to 65535.
.It Ic product , Ic company , Ic description , Ic copyright No = Ar string
Its
.Ql ProductName ,
.Ql CompanyName ,
.Ql FileDescription
and
.Ql LegalCopyright .
.El
.Pp
The program's manifest is
.Pa .aqr/sfx/manifest.xml
where there is one, as it is; else one made of
.Ic admin
and
.Ic subsystem ,
for Windows 7 to 11, aware of each monitor's DPI and of Common Controls 6.
.Ss \&[\&[shortcut\&]\&]
Each a shortcut made once the files are written, before the program is run.
Not with
.Ic run.cleanup .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic target No = Ar path
A file of the archive (not in
.Pa .aqr/ ) .
Required.
.It Ic name No = Ar text
The shortcut's name
.Pq Ar name Ns Pa .lnk .
Required.
.It Ic at No = Qo Cm desktop Qc | Qo Cm start-menu Qc
On the desktop or among the programs of the start menu.
Required.
.It Ic folder No = Ar path
A folder of the start menu's programs it is in
.Pq Cm start-menu No alone .
.It Ic args No = [ Ar arg ... ]
The arguments it gives the target.
.It Ic description No = Ar text
Its comment.
.It Ic all-users No = Ar bool
Of all users, not the user's alone (false); only of a program run as an administrator
.Pf ( Ic pe.admin ,
or
.Pa manifest.xml ) .
.El
.Sh THE PROGRAM
.Nm program
.Op Fl y
.Op Fl -noexec
.Op Fl -keep
.Op Ar dir
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar dir
Where the files go, in place of
.Ic extract.dest
.Pf ( Ic extract.subdir
and
.Ic extract.ask
then do nothing).
.It Fl y , Fl -yes
Ask nothing: a file there is written over where it would be asked.
.It Fl -noexec
Run nothing once the files are written (and write out
.Pa .aqr/
too).
.It Fl -keep
Leave the files where they would be removed once the program ran.
.It Fl h , Fl -help , Cm /?
Show a summary of the options.
.El
.Pp
It ends with 0 where done (or the exit code of the program run, with
.Ic run.exit-code ) ,
1 where it failed, and 2 where the prompt, the license or the question of where the files go
was declined.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Of the program, for tests:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev AQR_SFX_LANG
The language tag taken in place of the user's.
.It Ev AQR_SFX_SHORTCUTS
A directory where the shortcuts are made in place of the desktop and the start menu.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
An installer, run as an administrator:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
title = "Tool 1.2"

[extract]
dest = "{programs}/Tool"
ask = true

[ui]
prompt = { en = "Install Tool 1.2?", ko = "Tool 1.2를 설치할까요?" }
license = "license.txt"   # and license.ko.txt
banner = "banner.png"
finish = "Done."

[pe]
subsystem = "gui"
icon = "tool.ico"
admin = true
version = "1.2"
product = "Tool"
company = "Example"

[[shortcut]]
target = "bin/tool.exe"
name = "Tool"
at = "start-menu"
all-users = true
.Ed
.Pp
A program run from a temporary directory, removed once it ends:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[run]
program = ["setup.exe", "/dir", "{dest}"]
window = "hidden"
.Ed
.Pp
Made, and signed once made (on Windows, whose shell is
.Li cmd ) :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
> aqr --format sfx -o tool.exe --run-after "signtool sign /a \e\(dq%AQR_OUTPUT%\e\(dq" tool
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr aqr 1 ,
.Xr aqrattributes 5
.Sh CAVEATS
The archive in a self-extracting program is not edited
.Pf ( Fl a ,
.Fl s ,
.Fl -delete ,
.Fl -compact
of
.Xr aqr 1 ) :
extract it and make the program again.
Signing must come last, since bytes appended break the signature.
